From: OpenAI ChatGPT/Codex (GPT-5) <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: as21xxx: defer DT probe while firmware loader is busy

Runtime on r0+37893-6f8eae077c shows the BPI-R4 Pro 8X LAN-side
AS21010PB1 still being selected too early:

  Aeonsemi AS21010PB1 mdio-bus:18: firmware loader busy, retrying for up to 15000 ms
  Aeonsemi AS21010PB1 mdio-bus:18: firmware loader stayed busy after 15000 ms
  Aeonsemi AS21010PB1 mdio-bus:18: probe ... failed with error -22

After that hard probe failure, the same MDIO device is claimed by the
Generic Clause 45 PHY driver and never gets another AS21xxx probe.  The
WAN-side AS21010PB1 then succeeds a few seconds later, which means the
problem is not a missing firmware blob or a permanently dead PHY; the
driver returned a permanent error for a temporary loader-busy condition.

Use the kernel's normal probe-deferral mechanism for this case.  Keep a
short local retry window for transient loader races, then return
-EPROBE_DEFER from probe if the loader is still busy.  This prevents the
Generic Clause 45 fallback from permanently stealing the DT-declared
AS21010PB1 node and lets the driver core retry the concrete AS21xxx
driver after the rest of the MDIO/DSA stack has progressed.

This does not hide persistent failure: repeated deferred probes will
still log the busy state, and non-busy firmware/IPC errors keep returning
their real error code.

Adapted-by: OpenAI ChatGPT/Codex (GPT-5)
---
 drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c
@@ -196,7 +196,7 @@
 #define AEON_IPC_TIMEOUT		(AEON_IPC_DELAY * 200)
 
 #define AEON_FW_LOAD_RETRY_DELAY_MS	500
-#define AEON_FW_LOAD_RETRY_TIMEOUT_MS	15000
+#define AEON_FW_LOAD_RETRY_TIMEOUT_MS	3000
 #define AEON_IPC_DATA_NUM_REGISTERS	8
 #define AEON_IPC_DATA_MAX		(AEON_IPC_DATA_NUM_REGISTERS * sizeof(u16))
 
@@ -466,7 +466,7 @@
 	if (ret == -EBUSY) {
 		phydev_err(phydev, "firmware loader stayed busy after %u ms\n",
 			   elapsed_ms);
-		return -EINVAL;
+		return -EBUSY;
 	}
 
 	if (ret)
@@ -727,6 +727,8 @@
 			    "firmware IPC not ready during config_init, reloading\n");
 
 		ret = aeon_firmware_load_wait(phydev);
+		if (ret == -EBUSY)
+			return -ENODEV;
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
 
@@ -777,6 +779,11 @@
 	    of_find_property(phydev->mdio.dev.of_node,
 			     "firmware-name", NULL)) {
 		ret = aeon_firmware_load_wait(phydev);
+		if (ret == -EBUSY) {
+			phydev_warn(phydev,
+				    "firmware loader still busy, deferring probe\n");
+			return -EPROBE_DEFER;
+		}
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
 	}
